# D.Ai Server (docs/SERVER.md §2, §4): no desktop, no graphical apps, no local AI, no voice, no browser.
# Administration is over SSH with keys only; everything else is a service the organisation adds on purpose.

# Remote administration, key-only (openssh-server; the hardened settings are in includes.chroot_after_packages)
openssh-server
# Repeated failed SSH logins are banned for a time
fail2ban
# Audit trail of logins, privilege use and changes to configuration (rules in includes.chroot_after_packages)
auditd
# File-integrity baseline, checked daily (rules in includes.chroot_after_packages)
aide
# Time, from the organisation's own source (none is chosen by the image)
chrony
# Password quality rules
libpam-pwquality
# Encrypted backups (the D.Ai Backup tooling comes in a later stage)
restic
